why async awaits exist before this handing async code with the promise looked like this 

fetchData()
  .then((data) => {
    console.log(data);
    return processData(data);
  })
  .then((result) => {
    console.log(result);
  })
  .catch((err) => {
    console.log(err);
  }); 

  async and awaits are used to handle asynchronus operations in a cleaner way and more relaiable way 

  asynchronus operations are task that takes times like
  .fetching data from the apis 
  .reading files 
  .connecting database 
  .waiting for the payment confirmation
  .uploading an image 
  instead of waiting or blocking the program js continues running the other code while waiting 


  before async/awaits
  "call backs" 
  "promises" 
  this works but when many  async operations are chained, code become harder to read

  